def summarize(nums):
    # Return None for [], else {'count', 'min', 'max', 'mean'}
    ...

solution:
def summarize(nums):
    if not nums:
        return None
    count = len(nums)
    return {
        'count': count,
        'min': min(nums),
        'max': max(nums),
        'mean': round(sum(nums) / count, 2),
    }

One pass over the list per built-in: O(n) time, O(1) extra space. Returning None (not an empty dict) makes 'no data' impossible to confuse with real statistics.

